WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:13.260
Malcolm Grant: Good morning, ladies and gentlemen, to the meeting of the Board of NHS England in London.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.440
To the meeting we welcome members of the public
who have joined us here, and also those who

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:23.500
are watching the meeting on our live stream.
We are committed to the openness and transparency

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.580
of the conduct of our business, especially
the formal decision-making that will be taking

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:33.890
place this morning. However, I should emphasise,
as I always do, that it is a meeting in public,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.050
not a public meeting; also, that the Board
does a great deal of its work not in formal

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.750
meetings such as this but in its thinking
around strategy and development sessions.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.780
So, for example, yesterday afternoon we spent
time in a development session on the theme

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:55.270
of personalised medicine and, in particular,
the whole genomes project, which is being

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:59.930
run by Genomics England Ltd in partnership
with us, and trying to understand what would

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:05.979
be the implications for the NHS over future
years of moving to a model which is more closely

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:12.520
focused on personalisation of medicine.
We will this afternoon be moving into a private

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:19.140
session, and the agenda for this afternoon
will include a scrutiny of the draft annual

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.619
report and accounts, which we have to take
in private session because they do not become

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:28.780
public until they are laid before Parliament.
We will also be doing a preliminary evaluation

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:34.900
of our performance against the mandate, which
again will require a full report in due course.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.920
So there is a clear distinction between the
public business and the private business of

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.700
the Board.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.180
Next issue is to report apologies. We have

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:02.619
apologies for this morning only from Wendy
Becker, who has an unfortunate clash with

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:07.850
other Board obligations, but she was with
us yesterday for the development session.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.940
I want to just touch upon two or three preliminary

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:18.310
matters this morning. First of all, the issue
of declarations of interest. I am keen to

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:23.889
introduce a custom and habit on the Board
that, at each of the meetings, we will table

00:02:23.889 --> 00:02:30.530
a written statement of the interests held
by members of the Board of NHS England. This

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:35.900
is, I think, as part of a general practice
that we would wish to employ in order to raise

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:42.230
the consciousness across the whole of the
health sector about the importance of identifying

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:47.130
interests, identifying potential conflicts
of interest and managing those in the way

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:52.340
in which business is conducted. That is the
theme of the task and finish group that I

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.220
have been asked to chair, which will be looking
at this issue across the whole of the NHS.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.230
We will be coming today to look at conflicts
of interest in relation to CCGs, and there

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.590
will be a report on that specific aspect of
the business.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:11.440
So may I pause at this stage and ask whether
any member of the Board has any interest which

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.130
is in potential conflict with anything on
the agenda today?

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.239
Victor Adebowale: No conflict, Chair, but
just for the record I should add that I am

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:22.190
a board member of Co-op Group. It does not
appear on here.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.040
Malcolm Grant: Yes, we will add that to the
list.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.609
John Burn: Chair, I should also just mention
something.

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:33.239
Malcolm Grant: I am sorry?
John Burn: Since it was specifically discussed

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:39.880
in the Daily Telegraph in the case of the
Archbishop, NorthGene, which I help run, is

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:45.760
actually part of QuantuMDx Group. It is not
named in my list of interests. It is a paternity

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.160
testing company.
Malcolm Grant: Okay, well, thank you. We will

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.699
take note of that. Thank you very much.

00:03:50.699 --> 00:03:56.669
I have got a couple of issues to raise in
relation to the executive team. The first

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:02.349
is to report that, when Simon Stevens joined
us as Chief Executive a little over two years

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:08.019
ago, it was against a contract which provided,
as you would expect, for a number of issues.

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:11.479
However, two of them in particular I need
to mention this morning. The first was the

00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:15.669
question of salary, and the second was the
question of bonus.

00:04:15.669 --> 00:04:21.209
On the question of salary you may recall that,
on his appointment, Simon voluntarily took

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:27.860
a percentage reduction in his salary. At each
of his performance reviews thereafter – at

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.400
each succeeding year – I have raised with
him that question as to whether he would now

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.990
wish to revert to the salary for which we
have made provision, and I have to report

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:46.190
formally this morning that he has maintained
his original position and will take a £20,000

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:51.950
reduction. I can keep bidding this up.
Simon Stevens: Voluntary endeavour, really.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:56.960
Yes, just a joy and a pleasure.
Malcolm Grant: Yes. Well, we know all of that,

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.800
but he will take a £20,000 reduction on his
salary. As you would expect, his answer to

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.740
me on the question of bonus was that he would
not wish to be considered for a bonus. So

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.180
I wish that to be recorded formally, and our
thanks to Simon accordingly.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.660
Appointment of Matthew Swindells
Secondly in relation to the executive team,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.210
I wish to report that this will be the last
meeting of Richard Barker, who has been standing

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:25.240
in to the position that was vacated by Barbara
Hakin, but at the end of this month we will

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.990
be joined by Matthew Swindells. I would just
like, on behalf of the Board, Richard, to

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:34.170
thank you for what you have done. It has been
an extraordinary job in a very complex and

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:39.090
turbulent time, and we have been grateful
to you for your wise counsel and advice. Thank

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:41.280
you very much.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:47.590
A couple of governance issues. First, to report
to the Board and to seek the Board’s endorsement

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:53.430
of the appointment to the Audit and Risk Assurance
Committee of Gerry Murphy, who is currently

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:58.490
chairman of the audit committee of the Department
of Health. He has been attending our Audit

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:04.730
and Risk Assurance Committee as an observer
and participant, and I know, David, you are

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:09.450
keen, as am I, to formalise that relationship
and to appoint him formally to the Committee.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:14.240
I am assuming that that is agreed around the
table? Thank you.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:20.260
Also to report that Wendy Becker, who has
been recently appointed as one of our non‑executives,

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:24.010
will join ARAC, and she will also join the
Investment Committee.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.500
I want also, in connection with this, to report

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:35.990
the appointment of Noel Gordon to be the new
chair of NHS Digital, and extend to him, I

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:44.340
think, our congratulations on taking on such
an extraordinary, important role: to look

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:53.270
forward to ever-closer working relationships
with NHS Digital, formerly HSCIC, and to advise

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:58.870
also that Noel will, as a consequence, come
off the Investment Committee but has agreed

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:04.300
to remain on ARAC and to chair specialised
commissioning and remain on the Commissioning

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:09.060
Committee.
I would also like publicly to pay tribute

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:15.930
to Kingsley Manning, who has now stood down
and finished his term as the chair of HSCIC,

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:22.260
and to say how much we are looking forward
to working with NHS Digital, as it now is,

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.800
in its new guise.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:32.100
Finally on governance matters, to let everybody
be aware that we will be holding our AGM on

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:38.139
25th October. The Board will be involved in
a time‑out activity through the rest of

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:44.900
that day, but in the evening please could
you hold the date, as we say, for our AGM.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:51.340
Finally, a couple of items of activity. First,

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:57.180
to advise the Board that I have advised a
new, informal advisory council of chairs of

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:04.580
CCGs to help me understand what is happening
in their activities. We held our first meeting

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:12.010
on 29th April. It was a very open discussion,
and, for me, immensely rewarding. We will

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:16.680
have another meeting in October, and I am
happy to invite any non-executive member of

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:20.730
the Board who would wish to join me on that
occasion to do so. We will get that into people’s

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:26.270
diaries.
Then, finally, to let the Board know that

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:33.789
on 6th June I will be leading a UKTI/Healthcare
UK trade mission to India on the theme of

00:08:33.789 --> 00:08:40.300
health. That is partly in my capacity as chair
of this Board, but also partly in my capacity

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:48.010
as a UK business ambassador. It is, I think,
a very interesting time for health-related

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:51.690
industry within the UK to be engaging with
India, and vice versa.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:55.940
So that, I think, brings me to the end of

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:01.020
my preliminary matters, and if there are no
observations or comments on the Chairman’s

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:08.080
report, may I move then to the minutes of
the previous meeting? I am assuming that everybody

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:13.710
has read them, and that you are happy to endorse
them. I have no matters arising, and I do

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:17.460
not see any indication of others with matters
arising,

